.TH WHISKER 1 "2026" "ChonkOS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
whisker \- socket, network, firewall lease and drift inspection
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B whisker
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.I command
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B whisker
lists listening sockets with their owners, manages expiring nftables firewall
leases, detects listener drift against a saved baseline, terminates processes
bound to a port, and reports network status. Exit status is 0 on success and
1 on any error; \fBwatch\fR exits 1 on timeout and \fBdrift\fR exits 2 when
CRITICAL changes are found.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-json
Print machine-readable JSON on stdout instead of a table.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR ports " [\fB\-\-all\fR]"
List listening sockets from /proc/net/{tcp,tcp6,udp,udp6} with owner PID and
process name; each row is tagged exposed, local or interface. \fB\-\-all\fR
includes sockets in other states.
.TP
.BR lease " add PORT \fB\-\-for\fR DURATION [\fB\-\-proto\fR tcp|udp]"
Insert PORT into the native nftables set chonkos_leases_tcp or
chonkos_leases_udp (table inet chonkos_filter) with a kernel-side timeout
(10 s to 24 h); the entry expires on its own and is gone after a reboot.
Requires root. With \fB\-\-json\fR prints
{"status":"added","proto":"tcp","port":8080,"timeout":1800}.
.TP
.BR lease " list"
List active leases with timeout and remaining seconds. Requires root.
With \fB\-\-json\fR prints
{"leases":[{"proto":"tcp","port":8080,"timeout":1800,"expires":1712}]}.
.TP
.BR lease " revoke PORT [\fB\-\-proto\fR tcp|udp]"
Remove a lease immediately. Requires root. With \fB\-\-json\fR prints
{"status":"revoked","proto":"tcp","port":8080}.
.TP
.BR baseline " [\fB\-\-save\fR]"
Snapshot the current listening sockets (protocol, bind address, port, scope,
owning executable). \fB\-\-save\fR atomically writes
/var/lib/chonkos/whisker-baseline.json and requires root.
.TP
.B drift
Compare current sockets against the saved baseline; exits 2 on CRITICAL
changes (for example a new exposed port), 0 otherwise. With \fB\-\-json\fR
prints {"status":"clean|drift|uninitialized","changes":[...]}.
.TP
.BR kill " PORT [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-\-yes\fR]"
Terminate the processes listening on PORT: SIGTERM by default, SIGKILL with
\fB\-\-force\fR. Asks y/N first unless \fB\-\-yes\fR. PID 1, PID 0, the tool's
own PID and OpenSSH server processes are protected. Exits 1 when no
listener is found or the owner is hidden (try sudo).
.TP
.B net
Report active interfaces and addresses, default gateway, DNS nameservers,
Tailscale backend state, and TCP latency to 1.1.1.1:53 in milliseconds.
.TP
.BR watch " HOST:PORT [\fB\-\-timeout\fR SECONDS] [\fB\-\-interval\fR MS]"
Wait for a TCP connection to HOST:PORT. Defaults: timeout 60 s, interval
500 ms. Exits 0 with {"open":true} when the port opens, 1 with
{"open":false} on timeout.
.SH .local RESOLUTION
The whisker binary is statically linked against musl, so glibc NSS modules
(including mDNS) are unavailable and hostnames under \fB.local\fR cannot be
resolved by the tool itself. \fBnet\fR and \fBwatch\fR detect failed
\fB.local\fR lookups, report this limitation, and suggest using a direct IP
address or the systemd-resolved stub at 127.0.0.53.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
whisker ports
.TP
whisker --json ports --all
.TP
sudo whisker lease add 8080 --for 30m
.TP
sudo whisker --json lease list
.TP
sudo whisker lease revoke 8080
.TP
sudo whisker baseline --save
.TP
whisker --json drift
.TP
whisker kill 8080
.TP
whisker kill 8080 --yes
.TP
whisker net
.TP
whisker net printer.local
.TP
whisker watch 192.168.1.10:22 --timeout 10
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/chonkos/whisker-baseline.json
Saved socket baseline used by \fBdrift\fR.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nap (1),
.BR chonk (1)
